13. In botanical and zoölogical copy, the names of species if derived from proper names or from generic names, but in geological and medical matter use lower case for the names of species, even though derived from proper names: e.g., Clover-root Borer,
                        Hylesinus trifolii,
                        Pterygomatopus schmidti.  {24}

1. The word State when it refers to a political division of the Union: e.g., the State 
                        {25}
                          of Massachusetts; but use lower case when the word is employed as an adjective.

7. Scripture references should be spaced as follows: II Sam. 
                  1 : 2–6;

                  2 : 8–12.

